<configs>

	<!--
		=====================================================================
		 KitsuneLearnedSkills - remove crafting-skill magazines
		=====================================================================

		All 24 crafting skills have a learn-by-doing source now:
		  XML (Config/buffs.xml)         learn by using   - 16 skills
		  DLL (KitsuneLearnedSkills.dll) learn by crafting - all 24, read from
		                                 each craftable's UnlockedBy property,
		                                 plus doing-hooks for the lines whose
		                                 first craftable sits above level 1

		TWO DELIBERATE EXCEPTIONS keep their magazines, so they have both
		paths: armorSkillMagazine and backpackSkillMagazine.

		BACKPACKS (0.9.0): craftingBackpack is a 24th skill the mod originally
		missed. The sweep below caught its Pack Rat magazine anyway, which
		stranded it: the first backpack recipe unlocks at level 5, so crafting
		could never start it. The DLL now levels it from opening fresh loot
		containers, and the magazine is kept as a safety net until that is
		proven in play. Once it is, delete the
		not(@name='backpackSkillMagazine') clauses here and in traders.xml.
		None of its 7 loot groups go empty from that alone (armor's magazine
		is the last survivor in 4 of them), so no filler is needed until both
		holdouts are dropped.

		ARMOR: craftable armor does not carry UnlockedBy directly. It inherits it
		through Extends:
		    armorPrimitiveHelmet -> armorPrimitiveMaster [UnlockedBy=craftingArmor]
		The game merges Extends properties at load, so the DLL should see it at
		runtime, but that cannot be proven by reading the XML. Keeping the
		magazine means armor cannot be stranded even if that assumption is
		wrong. Once armor is confirmed to level by crafting, delete the
		not(@name='armorSkillMagazine') clause below and add its 10 groups back
		to the filler list.

		Seeds and traps needed the DLL's block fallback: they exist only as
		BLOCKS (plantedCotton1, dartTrap, autoTurret) and carry UnlockedBy on
		the block rather than the item. Both are craftable, so both are covered.

		Perk books live in their own groups and are never touched.
		KitsuneSharedReading shares them across the party.

		History: 0.2.0 emptied one group (23 of 218 entries). 0.3.0 swept all
		218 but stranded 7 skills. 0.4.0 scoped to the 16 the XML covered.
		0.5.0 added the 5 the DLL covered. 0.6.0 covers everything except the
		deliberate armor holdout: 211 of 218 removed.

		0.7.0 postscript: 0.6.0's "all 23 have a source" claim was wrong for
		five lines (Workstations, Vehicles, Seeds, Electrician, Traps) — their
		learn-by-crafting source existed but sat entirely ABOVE the first
		unlock level (forge at Workstations 4, dart trap at Traps 25, ...), so
		with magazines gone those skills were stranded at level 1. 0.7.0's DLL
		closes the gap with doing-hooks that work from level 1: workstation
		queue completions (campfire counts), vehicle repairs, wire-tool
		connections, and always-unlocked gateway crafts (spikes/barbed fence
		for Traps, farm plots for Seeds). Magazines stay removed.
	-->

	<remove xpath="//lootgroup/item[contains(@name,'SkillMagazine') and not(@name='armorSkillMagazine') and not(@name='backpackSkillMagazine')]"/>

	<!--
		These 10 groups held nothing but removed magazines and would be left
		empty. Some are force-picked by their containers, so pay out dukes.
	-->
	<append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='weaponSkillMagazinesOnly']"><item name="casinoCoin" count="5,25"/></append>
	<append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupWorkingStiffsMagazines']"><item name="casinoCoin" count="5,25"/></append>
	<append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupQuestT1SkillMagazineBundle']"><item name="casinoCoin" count="25,75"/></append>
	<append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupBuriedSuppliesT1_03']"><item name="casinoCoin" count="5,25"/></append>
	<append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupMoPower02']"><item name="casinoCoin" count="5,25"/></append>
	<append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupPassNGasMagazines']"><item name="casinoCoin" count="5,25"/></append>
	<append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupZpackNurse02']"><item name="casinoCoin" count="5,25"/></append>
	<append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupShotgunMessiahCrateMagazines']"><item name="casinoCoin" count="5,25"/></append>
	<append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupShamwayMagazines']"><item name="casinoCoin" count="5,25"/></append>
	<append xpath="//lootgroup[@name='groupPopNPillsMagazines']"><item name="casinoCoin" count="5,25"/></append>

</configs>
